CONTEXT AnchorTest
-- Reproducer from https://github.com/AmpersandTarski/Ampersand/issues/562:
-- the violation term of the |--direction of this ENFORCE is
--   x /\ (-a \/ -(f;st~)) /\ -((I-f;f~);a)
-- in which x is a complement-free member ("anchor"). The anchored rewrite
-- must compile every complement as an anti-join bounded by x; without it,
-- the generated SQL enumerates the Cartesian product V[S*E] twice.
RELATION x[S*E]
RELATION a[S*E]
RELATION f[S*T] [UNI]
RELATION st[E*T] [UNI]
ENFORCE x := (a /\ f;st~) \/ (I[S] - f;f~);a
ENDCONTEXT
